      "id": "theverge-2026-07-28-save-150-on-this-smart-indoor-bike-trainer-that-can-keep-you",
      "title": "Save $150 on this smart indoor bike trainer that can keep you riding during the off months",
      "summary": "While the summer months are great for putting in the miles on your favorite bike, it can be frustrating to have to hang it up when the weather turns. This smart bike trainer turns your road bike into an indoor exercise bike, with Wi-Fi and Bluetooth to connect to your PC, iOS, or Android device, and support for a wide variety of interactive and training apps. Multiple retailers have the Kickr Core",
      "body": "While the summer months are great for putting in the miles on your favorite bike, it can be frustrating to have to hang it up when the weather turns. This smart bike trainer turns your road bike into an indoor exercise bike, with Wi-Fi and Bluetooth to connect to your PC, iOS, or Android device, and support for a wide variety of interactive and training apps. Multiple retailers have the Kickr Core 2 on sale for $399.99 (usually $549.99) in both the Cog and Click version (Wahoo, Amazon) which fits 8-13 speed bikes, and the version with an included 11-speed cassette (Wahoo, Amazon).\n[Product: Wahoo Kickr Core 2 | https://www.wahoofitness.com/devices/indoor-cycling/bike-trainers/kickr-core-2-buy, https://www.wahoofitness.com/devices/indoor-cycling/bike-trainers/kickr-core-2-zwift-cog-and-click-buy]\nOne of the main advantages to a trainer like the Kickr is access to dynamically adjustable resistance, which can work in concert with training apps to tune your workout, or interact with riding apps to replicate inclines and group rides. If you use heart rate or cadence trackers, the Kickr Core 2 can connect directly to them with ANT+ support, and the Cog and Click version includes controllers for changing your virtual gears that hook to your handlebars. I use mine to keep pedaling during the winter months in the Pacific Northwest, joining other cyclists from all over the world for group rides, challenges, and races using Zwift.\n* The Razer BlackShark V2 Pro is on sale at Amazon for $76.18, within a dollar of its all-time low price. This gaming headset has features designed for competitive gamers, including sound isolating ear cups to keep you focused, a wideband microphone so your teammates hear your callouts clearly, and a low-latency 2.4GHz connection. They’re compatible with PlayStation 4 and 5, PC, and mobile devices.\n* Costco members can grab the Dell Ultra Sharp 32-inch 6K monitor for $799.99, a $200 break from the usual price. While the 60Hz refresh and IPS panel aren’t exactly cutting-edge, the screen makes up for it with a super dense 6144 x 3456 resolution, where it has few direct competitors. This screen would be a great fit for an office setup, with a built-in webcam for taking meetings and KVM support for switching between multiple systems quickly. For connectivity, it supports HDMI and Mini DisplayPort at 6K, Thunderbolt 4, and 2.5GbE Ethernet.\n* Paper Mario: The Thousand Year Door for the Nintendo Switch 2 is on sale for $31.99 at Woot, almost half off the usual price of $59.99. This classic Gamecube game has been remastered for newer consoles, and sees you guiding a 2D version of Mario through a turn-based RPG where you’ll upgrade your abilities, solve puzzles, and fight a variety of enemies. It has a unique art style and gameplay elements you won’t find in other non-paper Mario games.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Deals",
        "Gadgets",
        "Verge Shopping"
      ],
