      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-28-elon-musk-s-x-money-app-is-rolling-out-in-the-us",
      "title": "Elon Musk’s X Money app is rolling out in the US",
      "summary": "Users get an X Visa debit card, which they can immediately add to Apple Pay and use to make instant peer-to-peer transfers within the app without fees or limits.",
      "body": "7:57 AM PDT · July 28, 2026\nX is launching its X Money app for paid X subscribers in the United States.\nUsers get an X Visa debit card, which they can immediately add to Apple Pay and use to make instant peer-to-peer transfers within the app without fees or limits. They will also receive a physical X Visa debit card that, according to X Money, has no foreign transaction fees and offers free cash withdrawals at worldwide ATMs.\nX Premium+ users (who pay $40 per month or $395 per year) are eligible for 6% APY, while Premium users (who pay $8 per month or $84 per year) can access the 6% rate if they link a direct deposit to their X Money account. X Money also says that users can get up to 3% cash back on certain purchases, and if they link a direct deposit, they can access that money a few days early.\nThe release of X Money reflects a decades-long dream for Elon Musk. In 1999, he founded X.com as a financial services startup, which later merged into PayPal. When he acquired Twitter in 2022, Musk changed the name of the platform to X and repurchased the X.com domain name.\nSince the Twitter acquisition, Musk has repeatedly stated that he wants to turn the social platform into an “everything app,” and the rollout of X Money is part of that ambition.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Amanda Silberling",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-28T14:57:12.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-10.24.40-AM.png?resize=1200,607",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/28/elon-musks-x-money-app-is-rolling-out-in-the-u-s/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
