      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-27-threads-users-can-now-chat-with-meta-ai-in-their-dms",
      "title": "Threads users can now chat with Meta AI in their DMs",
      "summary": "Meta on Monday said it is rolling out its Meta AI chatbot within Threads' DMs, giving users a way to chat with the AI assistant.",
      "body": "9:45 AM PDT · July 27, 2026\nImage Credits:Matthias Balk/picture alliance (opens in a new window) / Getty Images\nMeta on Monday said it is rolling out its Meta AI chatbot within Threads’ DMs, giving users a way to chat with the AI assistant.\nAlthough Threads users in select markets could already interact with Meta AI in public posts, like people can with Grok on X, this new integration lets users talk with the AI assistant privately.\nBy giving users an easier way to talk to an AI chatbot, Meta is looking to keep users within its ecosystem, with an eye toward discouraging them from using third-party assistants like OpenAI’s ChatGPT or Google Gemini.\nMeta AI is already available within DMs on Meta’s other platforms, including Facebook, Instagram, and WhatsApp.\nThe new integration lets users share Threads posts, images, links, and videos directly with Meta AI. You can ask follow-up questions and dive deeper into topics, too.\nThe update will be rolled out globally starting Monday, the company says.\nMeta noted it’s continuing to test Meta AI in Threads’ public feeds in a handful of global markets and is considering feedback before expanding availability more broadly. Users who want to see fewer Meta AI replies in their feed can mute @meta.ai, use the “Not interested” option on any Meta AI post, or hide Meta AI replies that appear on their post.\nBy further integrating Meta AI into Threads, Meta is positioning its X rival as a place where you can get information and recommendations without having to leave the app.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Aisha Malik",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-27T16:45:24.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/threads-finger-GettyImages-2232887912.jpg?w=1024",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/27/threads-users-can-now-chat-with-meta-ai-in-their-dms/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
