      "id": "bbc-2026-07-27-very-strong-tide-led-to-west-mersea-drownings-relative-says",
      "title": "Very strong tide led to West Mersea drownings, relative says",
      "summary": "Shahin Ahmed's seven-year-old son remains in a critical condition after being pulled from the water.",
      "body": "A mother and daughter who drowned off the Essex coast were swept out to sea by a \"very strong\" tide, a relative has said.Shahin Ahmed said six members of his family were paddling at West Mersea beach when they were knocked off their feet on Wednesday afternoon.Shelina Rahman, 41, and 15-year-old Sameeha, died in the tragedy, while Ahmed's seven-year-old son Musa was airlifted to hospital in a critical condition.Ahmed said his son, who is from east London, remained on a life support machine at a hospital in London.Three others were also taken to another hospital by ambulance after the incident. Ahmed said 12 of them were visiting West Mersea that day.\"This was 20 minutes before we were going to go home. The whole day, alhamdulillah (praise be to God), was really nice,\" Ahmed told Bangladeshi newspaper Surma News.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-27T12:50:38.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/0013/live/3408c450-86ad-11f1-8e17-395fea5a1d61.png",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3d3kj318vyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-07-27-mercedes-driver-scout-lagrue-to-join-red-bull",
      "title": "Mercedes driver scout Lagrue to join Red Bull",
      "summary": "The Mercedes driver scout involved in discovering Kimi Antonelli is leaving the team to join rivals Red Bull.",
      "body": "Red Bull have confirmed the appointment of the Mercedes driver scout involved in discovering Kimi Antonelli to head up their young driver programme.Frenchman Gwen Lagrue's move was revealed by BBC Sport earlier this month.On Monday, Red Bull released a statement announcing the 50-year-old's signing as director of their junior programme, adding he would join the team in 2027.Lagrue has been recruited essentially as a replacement for Helmut Marko, who retired from his long-time role as Red Bull's motorsport adviser at the end of last year. Red Bull team principal Laurent Mekies said in a statement: \"Gwen is one of the very best talent developers in F1 and I know first-hand the expertise, leadership and passion he brings to developing young drivers.\"The Red Bull Junior Programme has always been a cornerstone of Red Bull's success, and having Gwen lead it soon reflects the importance we continue to place on developing the next generation of F1 talent.\"Mekies paid tribute to Marko for his \"extraordinary contribution over more than two decades creating and leading the junior programme\", praising the Austrian former F1 driver's \"vision, commitment and ability to identify and develop exceptional talents\".Lagrue said in the statement: \"After 11 memorable years at Mercedes, I felt this was the right moment to take on a new challenge and continue growing personally and professionally.\"The Red Bull Junior Programme is one of the most respected and successful driver development programmes in motorsport.\"It has produced some of the greatest talents F1 has ever seen, and it is a real honour to have the opportunity to lead such a talented group of people and help shape its next chapter.\"Together, we have a fantastic framework to build on the programme's remarkable legacy, continue to evolve it for the future, and identify, develop and prepare the next generation of F1 race winners and World Champions, following a pattern Red Bull Racing has successfully repeated over the past 20 years.\"The Red Bull junior programme's most successful products have been four-time champion Sebastian Vettel and eight-time winner Daniel Ricciardo.Current Williams drivers Alex Albon and Carlos Sainz also came through the programme, although Albon was dropped in 2016 - after which he was given personal assistance by Lagrue - before being re-instated for his F1 debut in 2019.The announcement comes after Mercedes and Red Bull reached an agreement that has released Lagrue from his existing contract as driver development adviser to the Mercedes F1 team.At Mercedes, his role will be filled by a minor reshuffle of the existing young-driver programme, arguably the most effective in F1.Bradley Lord, who was already involved, was recently promoted to deputy team principal from his previous position as communications director and senior adviser to team principal Toto Wolff.And Mercedes have a team of up to 10 people analysing the junior categories, right down to the very junior levels of karting to find promising new talent.George Russell was Lagrue's first signing for the team following his appointment, a few months after the Briton famously approached Wolff and gave him a PowerPoint presentation arguing his case to be part of the Mercedes junior programme.The Briton has been supported by Mercedes since then as he completed the junior categories, was seconded to Williams for an F1 debut in 2019 and then promoted to Mercedes in 2022.Mercedes signed Antonelli when he was an 11-year-old racing in go-karts and he has been mentored by Mercedes through an accelerated programme that saw him replace Lewis Hamilton in the team when the seven-time champion joined Ferrari at the start of 2025.Antonelli is this year proving his billing as a generational talent in dominating the F1 world championship in only his second season.The 19-year-old has won five races and set six pole positions in 10 grands prix so far this season before Sunday's Belgian Grand Prix and is leading Russell by 25 points.Among other successes at Mercedes while Lagrue has been running the young-driver programme are Frenchman Esteban Ocon, who was their junior driver and has been managed by them through his 10-year career in F1 at Manor, Force India, Renault/Alpine and now Haas, and their current F1 reserve driver, the Dane Frederik Vesti.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-27T12:48:10.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/0648/live/bf3054e0-8364-11f1-a0d2-c70a9d6f1fff.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cvg7kdnv4p2o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 3,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-07-27-tv-presenter-and-comedian-bill-oddie-dies-at-85",
      "title": "TV presenter and comedian Bill Oddie dies at 85",
      "summary": "His agent pays tribute to the \"multi-talented\" broadcaster, comedian and conservationist.",
      "body": "Oddie was born in Rochdale, near Manchester, and grew up in Birmingham before attending Cambridge University, where he was a member of the illustrious Footlights comedy troupe.Before graduating, he was already writing for shows like satirical TV series That Was The Week That Was in the early 1960s.He went on to write and appear on programmes including I'm Sorry I'll Read That Again, At Last the 1948 Show, Twice a Fortnight and Doctor in The House.Often, he starred and wrote alongside other up-and-coming comedy names like Monty Python's John Cleese, Michael Palin and Terry Jones, and his fellow future Goodies - Tim Brooke-Taylor and Graeme Garden.Python star Eric Idle said he was \"very sad\" about the loss of Oddie.\"We watched England win the World Cup together at Wembley in '66. He was a very fine songwriter and I learned a lot from him,\" he wrote on X., externalThe Goodies got their own series in 1970, and the trio's slapstick comedy and madcap songs entertained millions of viewers for 12 years.Oddie was \"known as the hairy, cynical, anarchist member\" of the group, the BFI said, external, and his contribution also included writing novelty songs like The Funky Gibbon and The Inbetweenies, which both reached the UK top 10.Others paying tribute included actor and avid birdwatcher Samuel West, who wrote on X, external about the impact of watching Birding With Bill Oddie.\"Bill Oddie wore a great learning lightly, but he could never hide his enthusiasm,\" West said.\"His captivated, always improvised narration made that show the platonic ideal of natural history for me, and introduced a whole generation to the fascination of birds.\"Naturalist and author Stephen Moss posted that Oddie \"did more than anyone to popularise birding\".\"Very sad news of the death of Bill Oddie: birder, comedian, musician, artist and environmental campaigner, and dear friend and colleague to me and many others,\" Moss wrote, external.Oddie was a former vice president of the RSPCA, and the animal charity's current chief executive Jo Rowland said: \"I know many of our wildlife rescuers were inspired into animal welfare by Bill's groundbreaking broadcasting work and incredible knowledge of British birds, which brought the wonders of nature into millions of homes across the country.\"Nature has lost one of its best friends, fiercest champions and most iconic defenders.\"Our thoughts are with his family, friends, and the countless people he inspired to spend time birdwatching, to cherish nature, and to build a kinder world for animals.\"Reading FC also posted a tribute, external: \"A guest of honour at many matches down the years, he became a much-loved figure at the club.\"Bill's legacy will live on through his iconic chant among Royals supporters at the SCL Stadium and around the country for many years to come.\"Oddie was married to children's TV writer and artist Laura Beaumont. They have a daughter, Rosie, while Oddie and his first wife - singer and actress Jean Hart - had two daughters, Bonnie and Kate.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-27T12:47:47.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/fa5e/live/dc2c0720-89a8-11f1-a85a-79136c2d298e.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjejw8pq5elo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
