      "summary": "Highlights from the Esports World Cup in Paris and how to build a gaming PC.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live             Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food        Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live         Close menu\nA-ZTV GuideWatchlistHomeTech NowInside the Esports World CupTech Now - Inside the Esports World CupAndrew Rogers has the highlights from the Esports World Cup in Paris. Laura Cress learns how to build a gaming PC, and Shiona McCallum explores how AI is reshaping job recruitment. Duration25 minsFirst shown25 Jul 2026Available for 11 monthsAudio DescribedSign LanguageEpisodes EpisodesThis episodeInside the Esports World CupWWE: The Tech Behind the ShowAmmie Sekhon goes behind the scenes of WWE to see the tech that supports the show.Race for the Ultimate SupercomputerAdrienne Murray has rare access to Microsoft's Quantum Lab in Denmark.Adrienne Murray meets the team using technology to preserve a historic warship in Sweden.World Cup: Game-Changing TechShiona McCallum visits Fifa HQ in Zurich to see new tech being used in the World Cup.Shiona McCallum meets a medical expert testing out the future of prosthetics.Adrienne Murray explores how new 3D imaging is supporting heart procedures.Deep Dive: Underwater TechAndrew Rogers explores new tech trials helping people stay underwater for longer.Art Mystery: Can AI Solve It? Harriet Bradshaw finds out how AI is being used to help solve an art history mystery. Blenheim Palace: Can Tech Help to Restore it?Shiona McCallum tours Blenheim Palace, exploring the tech aiding its restoration.Climate Science in the CourtroomHow research linking climate change and extreme weather events is being used in lawsuits.Inside the High-Tech Insect FarmAlasdair Keane visits the underground insect farm turning food waste into animal feed.MWC Barcelona: What's New In Phone Tech?Paul Carter checks out the newest phones, gadgets and trends from MWC Barcelona. Norway's Fjords: Can Tourism Go Green?Alasdair Keane climbs aboard an electric boat in Norway.Inside Europe’s Space RaceAdrienne Murray visits the Esrange Spaceport in the extreme north of Sweden.Winter Olympics: Can Tech Boost Performance?Alasdair Keane visits the Olympic training centre in Oslo.Future Farming in AustraliaNick Kwek meets innovators using tech for Australia's agricultural industry.From Las Vegas, the latest trends and innovations at CES 2026.Jacqui Wakefield joins singer KT Tunstall as she sees her musical avatar.Space Exploration: Can Robots Lead the Way?Nick Kwek visits the National Space Industry Hub in Sydney.Icebreaker Tech: Navigating the ArcticAdrienne Murray meets the engineers designing icebreaker ship technology for the Arctic.Rising Seas: Can Tech Help Us Prepare?The scientists on a quest to improve our predictions of global sea level rise.Fixing Fashion's Sizing ProblemShiona McCallum meets an AI startup working to fix erratic clothing sizes in fashion.Movie Tech: Behind the ScenesAlasdair Keane explores a high-tech studio that transforms how car stunts are made.Brain Cells and BiocomputingZoe Kleinman meets the scientists trying to make living computers using brain cells.Cloud Seeding and Conspiracy TheoriesMarco Silva unpacks the science and technology of cloud seeding.IFA Berlin: The Rise of Smart TechAlasdair Keane explores the tech highlights at IFA Berlin.Lara Lewington explores the tech being trialled to find 'hidden' pancreatic cancer cases.Fighting Wildfires: Can Tech Help?How technology is bringing hope of earlier detection and prevention to wildfires.AI and the Future of HumanityJoe Tidy explores how the rise of artificial intelligence may play out.",
