    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-07-24-scott-overcomes-pressure-and-big-pal-dean-to-give-scotland-g",
      "title": "Scott overcomes pressure and big pal Dean to give Scotland golden start",
      "summary": "Scotland's Duncan Scott thrilled a home crowd with his swim to gold at Tollcross on the first full day of competition at the Commonwealth Games.",
      "body": "Scott was not being caught, though. Not tonight. Not here. Not with his Scotland kit on and his team looking to him to spark their Games.A Games which he has backed vocally since Glasgow salvaged it from the wreckage of Victoria's aborted bid.Almost exactly 12 years after he won his first Commonwealth medal in this very building, he was taking his 14th in his fourth Games. And it was going to be gold.\"I don't usually feel the expectation, but that one I probably did,\" he told BBC Sport Scotland. \"Simply because it's day one and I love representing Scotland and you want to try and get the whole team off to a good start.\"I think there was a bigger picture of trying to get good momentum for the crowd involvement for the rest of the week, and the team as well. So I felt that expectation, but it's nothing I couldn't deal with.\"You got the sense there was little that could have discomfited the Alloa native - a momentary loss of his accreditation apart - and even a post-race visit to the drugs testers wasn't going to trouble him.Scott's got the weekend off now - he's an old boy among the swimming set, after all - but he's more than done his bit to set Glasgow 2026 off on the right note.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
