    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-07-23-defoe-leaves-woking-after-eye-opening-first-managerial-role",
      "title": "Defoe leaves Woking after 'eye-opening' first managerial role",
      "summary": "Former England and Tottenham striker Jermain Defoe has described his first managerial job as an \"eye-opening experience\" following his departure from National League side Woking after just four months and nine matches in charge.",
      "body": "Former England striker Jermain Defoe has described his first managerial job as an \"eye-opening experience\" following his exit from National League side Woking after just four months and six league games in charge.The 43-year-old was named the replacement for Neal Ardley in March and won two of those six matches to guide the club to a 10th-placed finish last season. But on Thursday, Woking confirmed Defoe's stint had come to an abrupt end after they \"mutually agreed to part ways with immediate effect\" - two weeks before the opening match of the new campaign against Sutton United. \"Unfortunately, circumstances have ultimately made it impossible for me to continue in the position,\" Defoe said in an Instagram post.\"I am extremely proud of the work undertaken during my time at the club and genuinely felt that we were building something special.\"My time at Woking FC has been an eye-opening managerial experience and one that will undoubtedly make me stronger for the next challenge in my career.\"Defoe's ninth and final game in charge of Woking was a 1-0 defeat by Braintree Town in one of three pre-season friendlies on Tuesday.He scored 305 goals in 763 senior appearances for clubs including West Ham, Tottenham, Portsmouth and Sunderland before retiring in 2022. Defoe, who struck 20 times in 57 international appearances, was part of an interim coaching staff at Rangers in 2021 and then worked in the Spurs academy, before leaving in 2024 to pursue a full-time managerial role.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-23T21:02:11.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/3ef2/live/a5dd9620-86d3-11f1-8749-89447c313de6.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/c304d47ql6jo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
